  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Let f(X,Y)=⌈X+YX∣Y⌉f(X, Y) = \\left \\lceil \\dfrac{X + Y}{X | Y} \\right \\rceilf(X,Y)=⌈X∣YX+Y​⌉, i.e. the result of X+YX + YX+Y divided by X∣YX | YX∣Y rounded up, where ∣|∣ denotes the Bitwise OR symbol.\n\nYou are given an array AAA of length NNN.\n\nYour task is to compute ∑i=1N∑j=i+1Nf(Ai,Aj)\\sum_{i = 1}^{N} \\sum_{j = i + 1}^{N} f(A_i, A_j)∑i=1N​∑j=i+1N​f(Ai​,Aj​), i.e. the sum of fff over all pairs in the array AAA.\n\n**Note** : There is an additional constraint on the input that every number has at most **444 bits set** in their binary representation, i.e. it is possible to write Ai=2X1+2X2+...+2XLA_i = 2^{X_1} + 2^{X_2} + ... + 2^{X_L}Ai​=2X1​+2X2​+...+2XL​ with L≤4L \\le 4L≤4 and XiX_iXi​ are all non-negative integers.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line contains NNN - the size of the array.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,....,ANA_1, A_2, ...., A_NA1​,A2​,....,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the value of ∑i=1N∑j=i+1Nf(Ai,Aj)\\sum_{i = 1}^{N} \\sum_{j = i + 1}^{N} f(A_i, A_j)∑i=1N​∑j=i+1N​f(Ai​,Aj​).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai&lt;2301 \\le A_i \\lt 2^{30}1≤Ai​&lt;230",
      "AiA_iAi​ can be written as 2X1+2X2+....+2XL2^{X_1} + 2^{X_2} + .... + 2^{X_L}2X1​+2X2​+....+2XL​ with L≤4L \\le 4L≤4 and XiX_iXi​ non-negative integers.",
      "The sum of NNN does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105 over all test cases."
    ],
