      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n2\n1 2\n3\n1 1 1",
        "output": "1\n6",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : There is only one pair in the array i=1,j=2i = 1, j = 2i=1,j=2. So, we need to evaluate f(1,2)=⌈33⌉=1f(1, 2) = \\lceil \\frac{3}{3} \\rceil = 1f(1,2)=⌈33​⌉=1, as 1+2=1∣2=11 + 2 = 1 | 2 = 11+2=1∣2=1.\nTest Case 2 : It can be shown that f(1,1)=2f(1, 1) = 2f(1,1)=2, and there are 333 such pairs. Hence, the answer is 3⋅2=63 \\cdot 2 = 63⋅2=6."
      }
